#include <stdio.h>

double power(double base, int exponent){
    if (exponent == 0){
        return 1;
    }
    else {
        double temp = power(base, exponent / 2);
        // check if exponent is divisible by 2
        if (exponent % 2 == 0){
            return temp * temp; // even condition
        }     
        else {
            // odd condition
            if (exponent > 0){
                return base * temp * temp;
            }
            else {
                return (temp * temp) / base; // handling negative exponent
            }
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    double base = 2.0;
    int exponent = -7;
    double result = power(base, exponent);
    printf("Result: %.6lf\n",result);
    return 0;
}
```
This C program uses recursion to solve the power problem. It employs the divide and conquer methodology, which reduces the time complexity to O(log n) where n is the exponent, making the program more efficient. For handling negative exponents, the program divides the result by the base."}]

